  "review": {
    "basis": "Complete semantic reading of PROTOCOL.md followed by explicit allocation; line spans only locate reviewed clauses. No heading-to-module or keyword inference.",
    "preservation": "All baseline runtime content is retained verbatim; only SD-ORG-STRUCTURE-001 and SD-ORG-COORDINATION-001 add obligations. Existing scope, authority, exceptions, G0/G1 proportionality and non-authorizing examples are preserved. Maintainer-only edits are excluded from consumer source.",
    "formalization": "Structured boundaries refer to complete semantic clauses. They do not decide semantic judgments or manufacture facts. Formal bootstrap guards are necessary checks, not sufficient authorization.",
    "coreRationale": "Precedence, authority, proportionality, language, consumer exclusions, state separation and evidence invariants apply across routes. Entry/context/workspace add current identity and availability; conditional business modules remain on demand.",
    "dependencyRationale": "Dependencies are conservative prerequisites from reviewed meaning. Effectful branches add action/security/execution facets even when a request initially seems informational. Context assembly never grants authority. Organizational modeling also selects impact: its structural decision now explicitly requires the symmetric applicability clause in OOP-impact-propagation. This adds no authority, ticket or organization-type selector; unchanged G0 information/local-write routes stay lightweight. Material coordination selects execution through its actual action facets, alongside CI/change/impact context.",
    "limitations": [
      "Semantic review performed by the producing AI; no independent human/second-model approval claimed.",
      "No runtime adapter, provider enrollment or consumer installation executed by this package."
    ]
  },
